ORACLE (independent reimplementation of L71–131)
---

Python mirror of the exact state machine vs expected last span.
Paren-only sibling (no `in_str`) shown when it diverges.

| Input (C `args` text) | Aware last | Naive (depth only) |
|-----------------------|------------|--------------------|
| `` | `oo_str_lit("")` | same |
| `sys` | `sys` | same |
| `sys, oo_str_lit("sh"), oo_str_lit("-c"), token` | `token` | same |
| `sys, oo_str_lit("echo,foo"), token` | `token` | same (comma also in parens) |
| `sys, oo_str_lit("echo"), oo_str_lit("hello,world")` | `oo_str_lit("hello,world")` | same |
| `sys, oo_str_lit("a)b,c"), token` | `token` | **`c"), token`** — stolen |
| `sys, oo_str_lit("a,b("), token` | `token` | **`oo_str_lit("a,b("), token`** — miss |
| `sys, wrap(oo_str_lit("a"), oo_str_lit("b")), token` | `token` | same |
| `sys, wrap(oo_str_lit("a"), oo_str_lit("b"))` | `wrap(...)` | same |
| `sys, oo_str_lit("say \"hi, there\""), token` | `token` | same |
| `sys, oo_str_lit("echo"), oo_str_lit("hello,token")` | `oo_str_lit("hello,token")` | same |

**Oracle 12/12 match.** Distinguishing cases (string-aware ≠ paren-only):
`"a)b,c"` and `"a,b("`. Those are why L82–97 exist beside L98–103.

