RESIDUAL (honest; do not close)
---

1. **Check-path not paren-depth aware.**
   `c_secret_scan_call` stops at the **first** `RPAREN`. Isolated
   `sys_exec(sys, wrap("a", "b"), token)` : emit-c **BLOCK** (last-arg
   extracts `token`; scanner also sees IDENT `token`); `oodac check`
   prints `OK` (no `ERR\tsecret`). Fail-closed on emit. Dual-path secret
   does **not** hold when a previous argv is a call. Out of 7.2 last-arg
   OWN (would be check-path). Did not patch.

2. **Last-arg refuse is IDENT-only.**
   `c_arg_is_cap_ident` rejects quotes/parens. `sys_exec(sys, "sh", last)`
   with `last` a SECRET-bearing **call** (`wrap(token, x)`) is scanner
   (7.1), not this arm. Product last-argv contract for **bare IDENT**
   holds.

3. **7.1 scanner is a backstop** on full `args`. Last-arg is still the
   dedicated last-span IDENT refuse Domain A wired. B did not merge them.

4. **7.10** — `c_parse_secret_env` `name = name + c` still OPEN.

5. **`c_args_drop_first` is not string-aware** (same file L133–161).
   Used for `sys_exec` argv emit, not last-arg refuse. Not 7.2 OWN.

6. **`secret_sink_enforce_smoke` EXIT 1** — `secret_file_size_pass`
   annotation miss. sys_exec rails green. Same residual as Domain A.

7. **Full IFC / `${}` interp / macro-body SECRET** — `SECRET_TAINT.oot`.
   Not this last-arg contract.

